WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.140
The Gospel of Luke never names its author.

2
00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.700
It opens with one long,
polished Greek sentence,

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.260
addressed to a man called Theophilus.

4
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:11.720
The writer admits he was not there.

5
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:16.520
He relies on eyewitnesses, and on accounts
that many others had already written.

6
00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.430
And Theophilus means lover of God.

7
00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.990
So who wrote this Gospel, when,
and who was it meant to convince?

8
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.880
In this mission, you'll weigh
the clues for the author,

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:29.940
from early church writers
to the text itself.

10
00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.410
Then you'll place the
Gospel on a timeline,

11
00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:36.380
and see why scholars split
into early, middle and late.

12
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.530
Your mission: find out
who wrote Luke's Gospel,

13
00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.610
when, and who Theophilus
was meant to convince.
